      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Sonterra sits in northern Williamson County, just north of Jarrell, and I‑35 runs through it, linking it 27 miles north to Temple and 40 miles south to Austin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonterra%2C_Texas",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Residents and visitors enjoy numerous parks that showcase Texas’s open‑air recreation, offering hiking, picnicking, and birdwatching right in Sonterra.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/sonterra-45438",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Being close to Austin lets Sonterra residents tap into world‑class dining, entertainment, and cultural institutions while keeping a tranquil suburban feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
